<title>USA: Shurgard Storage Q1 FFO/shr rises to $0.56.</title>
<headline>Shurgard Storage Q1 FFO/shr rises to $0.56.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>SHURGARD STORAGE CENTERS, INC.</p>
<p>		    QUARTERLY OPERATING RESULTS (UNAUDITED)</p>
<p>		(Dollars in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>					 Three Months ended March 31,</p>
<p>					     1997	    1996</p>
<p> Revenue				$31,735	  $24,819</p>
<p> Net Operating Income (NOI)(A)   20,951	   15,878</p>
<p> Net Income			     9,197	    7,313</p>
<p> Funds From Operations (FFO)(B)  15,197	   12,196</p>
<p> FFO per Share(B)			0.56	     0.53</p>
<p> Regular Cash Dividends		0.48	     0.47</p>
<p>Weighted Average Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding		    27,362,137     23,196,858</p>
<p>NOTE: A) NOI is defined as rental revenue less direct property operating expenses and real estate taxes.</p>
<p>(B) In accordance with the recommendations of the National Association of Real Estate Investment Trusts (NAREIT), the Company modified its definition of FFO in 1995 to exclude amortization of financing costs resulting in reductions of $0.01 per share for the first quarter of both 1995 and 1996.</p>
</text>
